# Larkfield (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, section 3): the market town of the Larkdowns. Quick, a trader's speech; prices,
# weights and bargains. Drafts (phase 3), to be written properly with you (phase 7).

grammar larkfield
greet = Fair price to you | Good trade
greet.broad = Fair price, fair price
farewell = Good trading | Fair price
agree = Sold | Done
refuse = No sale | Not at that price
surprise = Well, sell me | There's a bargain
annoyed = Short-changed again | Scales and spite
very = top-weight
little = a lark's worth
good = fair-priced | full weight
bad = short-weighed | light
worthless = haggle-bait
luck = a bargain
child = lambkin
pet!! = my bargain | my lark
money = silver
nonsense = market talk
tag = , eh?
oath! = Scales and silver | By the market cross | Weights and measures
